# What must never enter a build context.
#
# Without this file `COPY . .` in the build stage copies the HOST's
# node_modules over the one `npm ci` just built inside the image. On a Windows
# host those workspace links do not survive the copy, so `tsc -b` fails with
# "File '@knowzy/tsconfig/node.json' not found" and "must have setting
# composite: true" — an error about the image that is really an error about the
# machine that built it. CI never saw it, because a fresh checkout has no
# node_modules; a developer building the same Dockerfile locally always did.
#
# Everything here is either rebuilt inside the image, environment-specific, or
# has no business in a production layer.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — regenerated by the build stage.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
out
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
coverage

# History and local configuration.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local adapter state. The mock question bank writes here; an image must start
# with an empty bank, not with whatever a developer last published.
fixtures/bank/.state

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
